CyberBot - Cybersecurity Awareness Chatbot
PROG Part 2 | IIE | 2026

Description

CyberBot is a WinForms GUI Cybersecurity Awareness Chatbot built with C# .NET 8.  
It expands the Part 1 console chatbot into a fully interactive graphical application that recognises cybersecurity keywords, detects user sentiment, remembers user details, and provides dynamic varied responses.

Features

Feature | Description

GUI Interface Dark-themed WinForms window with ASCII art logo, colour-coded chat, side panel buttons, and voice greeting
Keyword Recognition | Responds to 65+ cybersecurity topics including phishing, malware, passwords, VPNs, encryption, and more 
Random Responses | 5 varied responses per major topic — no two conversations feel the same 
Conversation Flow | Handles follow-up phrases like "tell me more", "another tip", "explain more" without restarting 
Memory & Recall | Remembers your name and favourite cybersecurity topic to personalise responses 
Sentiment Detection | Detects 15 moods (worried, curious, frustrated, overwhelmed, etc.) and adjusts responses accordingly 
Quiz | 3-round quiz with 15 questions across Basics, Threats, and Privacy topics 
Security Tips | 20 rotating security tips accessible via the side panel or by typing `tip` 
Error Handling | Rotating fallback responses for unrecognised input — never crashes on unexpected input 

Project Structure


CybersecurityChatbot/

├─GUI/
  ├── ChatForm.cs          Main WinForms GUI window
 └── QuizForm.cs          GUI quiz window (3 rounds, exit confirmation)

├── Core/
  ├── GUIChatEngine.cs     Core chat logic — state machine, memory, sentiment, responses
   └── QuizEngine.cs        Console quiz engine (Part 1, still compiles)

├── Data/
   ├── ResponseBank.cs      All keyword responses, tips, commands, conversational replies
  └── QuizBank.cs          15 quiz questions in 3 rounds

── Program.cs              Entry point — launches ChatForm

── PROG_Part1/              Legacy Part 1 classes (ChatEngine, DisplayHelper)

How to Run
Requirements
- Windows OS
- [.NET 8 SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet/8.0)
- Visual Studio 2022 (or later) or Visual Studio Code with C# extension

Steps

1.Clone the repository
   bash
   git clone https://github.com/rearabecwesekoto04/PROG_Part2.git
   cd PROG_Part2


2. Open the project  
   Open `CybersecurityChatbot.sln` in Visual Studio.

3. Build the project  
   Press `Ctrl + Shift + B` or go to Build → Build Solution.

4. Run the application  
   Press `F5` or click the Start button.  
   The CyberBot GUI window will launch automatically.

Usage

Getting Started
1. Launch the application — a voice greeting will play automatically.
2. Type your name in the input box and press Enter or click SEND.
3. Enter your favourite cybersecurity topic (e.g. `phishing`, `passwords`, `privacy`).
4. Start chatting! Ask any cybersecurity question or use the commands below.

Commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `help` | Show all available commands |
| `topics` | List all 65+ cybersecurity topics (select by number) |
| `tip` | Get the next security tip (cycles through 20 tips) |
| `quiz` | Launch the cybersecurity quiz |
| `history` | View your conversation history |
| `clear` | Clear the conversation history |
| `exit` | Exit the chatbot (confirmation dialog shown) |

Example Interactions

You:  Tell me about phishing
Bot:  Phishing attacks trick you into revealing sensitive info via fake 
      emails or websites. Always verify the sender's address...

You:  I'm worried about online scams
Bot:  I understand you're worried — here's what you need to know:
      If an offer sounds too good to be true, it almost certainly is...

You:  Tell me more
Bot:  Here's another tip about phishing, Rea:
      Hover over links before clicking to see the real URL...

You:  What do I like?
Bot:  As someone interested in phishing, Rea, here's something relevant...


Technologies Used

- Language: C# 
- Framework: .NET 8
- UI: Windows Forms (WinForms)
- Voice: System.Speech.Synthesis (SpeechSynthesizer)
- Data Structures: Dictionary, List (used throughout for all responses, moods, commands, colours)
- Patterns: OOP, State Machine, Dictionary of Delegates (Func\<string\>)

OOP & Code Design Highlights

- Dictionary of Delegates — commands map directly to handler methods (`Func<string>`), no long if/else chains
- Colour Dictionary — `Dictionary<string, Color>` manages the entire UI colour palette; one change updates everything
- Mood Dictionaries — three separate dictionaries handle mood detection, full mood responses, and short mood prefixes
- State Machine — `ChatState` enum controls conversation flow (`AwaitingName → AwaitingFavTopic → Active`)
- Thread Safety — voice greeting runs on `Task.Run()`; `InvokeRequired` ensures UI updates happen on the correct thread
- Exit Fix — `_forceClose` flag in `QuizForm` prevents `OnFormClosing` from blocking programmatic `Close()` calls

